  <!-- Services -->
  <section id="services" class="services-section">
    <h2>Our Services</h2>
    <p class="services-subtitle">Professional cleaning for every need</p>
    <div class="services-grid">
      <a href="/services/window-washing" class="service-card">
        <img src="/img/window_washing_image.png" alt="Window Washing" />
        <div class="service-card-body"><h3>Window Washing</h3><p>We ensure your windows are spotless, enhancing the clarity and beauty of your home.</p></div>
      </a>
      <a href="/services/screen-cleaning" class="service-card">
        <img src="/img/cover-slides/slide-4.png" alt="Screen Cleaning" />
        <div class="service-card-body"><h3>Screen Cleaning</h3><p>We remove built-up dust, pollen, dirt, and grime, leaving screens clean and clear.</p></div>
      </a>
      <a href="/services/solar-panel-cleaning" class="service-card">
        <img src="/img/solar_1.png" alt="Solar Panel Cleaning" />
        <div class="service-card-body"><h3>Solar Cleaning</h3><p>We clean solar panels to enhance your home's beauty and efficiency.</p></div>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- About / Guarantees -->
  <section id="about" class="about-section">
    <div class="about-grid">
      <div class="about-image"><img src="/img/water_pole_2.jpg" alt="Aloha Window Bros at work" /></div>
      <div class="about-content">
        <h2>Our Guarantees</h2>
        <div class="guarantee-item">
          <div class="guarantee-icon">✓</div>
          <div><h4>Your Satisfaction</h4><p>Before we leave, we walk around the property with you to ensure you absolutely love it.</p></div>
        </div>
        <div class="guarantee-item">
          <div class="guarantee-icon">⭐</div>
          <div><h4>High-Quality Service</h4><p>We use top-of-the-line tools including water-fed poles and pressurized screen cleaners.</p></div>
        </div>
        <div class="guarantee-item">
          <div class="guarantee-icon">💬</div>
          <div><h4>Customer Service</h4><p>Punctual arrivals, quick communication, and accommodating any specific requests.</p></div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Window Cleaning Ventura County (SEO context + internal links) -->
  <section class="county-section">
    <div class="county-inner">
      <div class="county-head">
        <span class="county-eyebrow">Ventura &amp; Santa Barbara County</span>
        <h2>Window Cleaning Ventura County, Coast to Conejo</h2>
        <p class="county-lede">
          Every neighborhood grows its own kind of grime. Salt spray on the coast, dry-season dust off the Conejo
          Valley, hard water almost everywhere. We read the glass before we touch it, then match the visit to your home.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="county-grid">
        <article class="county-card">
          <span class="county-icon" aria-hidden="true">🌊</span>
          <h3>On the coast</h3>
          <p>Salt air hazes the glass within weeks and creeps into frames and tracks if it sits. Coastal homes earn a shorter cycle than inland ones.</p>
          <ul class="county-links">
            <li><a href="/oxnard/">Oxnard</a></li>
            <li><a href="/ventura/">Ventura</a></li>
            <li><a href="/santa-barbara/">Santa Barbara</a></li>
          </ul>
        </article>

        <article class="county-card">
          <span class="county-icon" aria-hidden="true">🍃</span>
          <h3>Up the Conejo Valley</h3>
          <p>Dry-season dust and the Santa Anas load every pane and screen with grit, then the first rain streaks it all down the glass.</p>
          <ul class="county-links">
            <li><a href="/thousand-oaks/">Thousand Oaks</a></li>
            <li><a href="/simi-valley/">Simi Valley</a></li>
          </ul>
        </article>

        <article class="county-card">
          <span class="county-icon" aria-hidden="true">💧</span>
          <h3>Hard-water country</h3>
          <p>Sprinkler overspray leaves mineral spots that etch in under the sun. Purified water lifts them and dries without a single streak.</p>
          <ul class="county-links">
            <li><a href="/camarillo/">Camarillo</a></li>
            <li><a href="/ojai/">Ojai</a></li>
          </ul>
        </article>
      </div>

      <div class="county-foot">
        <p class="county-foot-copy">
          One trip covers all of it. Our four-in-one clean takes the windows, screens, frames, and sills together, and we can add
          <a href="/services/window-washing/">window washing</a>, <a href="/services/screen-cleaning/">screen cleaning</a>, and
          <a href="/services/solar-panel-cleaning/">solar panel cleaning</a> to the same visit.
        </p>
        <div class="county-guides">
          <a class="county-guide" href="/blog/window-cleaning-ventura-county-what-homeowners-should-know-before-hiring-professionals/">
            <strong>Before you hire anyone</strong><span>The Ventura County window cleaning guide</span>
          </a>
          <a class="county-guide" href="/blog/window-washing-ventura-county-why-professional-cleaning-makes-a-difference/">
            <strong>Why it lasts longer</strong><span>The window washing Ventura County guide</span>
          </a>
          <a class="county-guide" href="/blog/how-much-does-window-cleaning-cost-in-ventura-county/">
            <strong>What it costs</strong><span>Window cleaning prices for every city we serve</span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Window Cleaning Santa Barbara (South Coast context + internal links) -->
  <section class="sb-section">
    <div class="sb-inner">
      <div class="sb-head">
        <span class="sb-eyebrow">Santa Barbara County</span>
        <h2>Window Cleaning Santa Barbara, Where Glass Gets Hit From Both Sides</h2>
        <p class="sb-lede">
          Santa Barbara windows get loaded from two opposite directions on the same day. Onshore marine air lays a salt
          film down through the afternoon, then Sundowner winds fall off the Santa Ynez Mountains after dark and drop dry
          ridgeline dust straight on top of it. Aloha Window Bros cleans windows, screens, frames, and sills across
          <a href="/santa-barbara/">Santa Barbara</a>, Montecito, Hope Ranch, and Goleta, and most homes here quote
          between $200 and $475 for the complete four-in-one clean.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="sb-body">
        <article class="sb-block">
          <h3>Sundowners arrive when the wind should be dying down</h3>
          <p>
            A Sundowner is a downslope windstorm that forms on the lee side of the Santa Ynez Mountains and spills onto
            the Santa Barbara coastal plain, peaking from early evening to mid-morning. The National Science Foundation
            funded a full field campaign to study them, the Sundowner Winds Experiment, run out of Santa Barbara between
            April 1 and May 15 of 2022. The practical version for a homeowner: a house washed at noon on the Riviera or
            in Mission Canyon can carry visible grit by breakfast. Do not dry dust that film. It is mineral grit, and a
            dry cloth grinds it across the glass.
          </p>
        </article>

        <article class="sb-block">
          <h3>Nobody can quote you a Santa Barbara water hardness number, including us</h3>
          <p>
            Most cities we serve run on one supply and one mineral profile. The City of Santa Barbara runs on as many as
            eight, and the mix is rebuilt every water year. In water year 2025, which ran from October 2024 through
            September 2025, the city drew nothing at all from the State Water Project and nothing from groundwater, while
            17 percent of its water came out of the Charles E. Meyer Desalination Plant. When a company quotes you a fixed
            grains-per-gallon figure for Santa Barbara, they are quoting a number that already moved last year and will
            move again. We read the deposit on your glass and treat what is actually on it.
          </p>
        </article>
      </div>

      <div class="sb-table-wrap">
        <p class="sb-table-caption">
          City of Santa Barbara water supply by source, water year 2025. Total production 11,777 acre-feet.
        </p>
        <div class="sb-table-scroll">
          <table class="sb-table">
            <thead>
              <tr><th scope="col">Source of supply</th><th scope="col">Share</th><th scope="col">WY 2025 volume</th></tr>
            </thead>
            <tbody>
              {sbWaterRows.map((r) => (
                <tr><th scope="row">{r[0]}</th><td>{r[1]}</td><td>{r[2]}</td></tr>
              ))}
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="sb-sources">
          Sources:
          <a href="https://santabarbaraca.gov/sites/default/files/2026-02/2025_Water_Supply_Mgmt_Report.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">City of Santa Barbara, 2024-2025 Water Supply Management Report</a>,
          <a href="https://santabarbaraca.gov/government/departments/public-works/water-resources/water-system/water-sources" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">City of Santa Barbara Water Sources</a>,
          <a href="https://www.eol.ucar.edu/field_projects/swex" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">NCAR Earth Observing Laboratory, Sundowner Winds Experiment</a>.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="sb-foot">
        <p class="sb-foot-copy">
          Our <a href="/santa-barbara/">Santa Barbara window cleaning page</a> carries the full picture: recommended
          service intervals by zone, from the Mesa and the waterfront through Montecito, Hope Ranch, Mission Canyon, and
          Goleta, plus what a salt haze actually is and why it comes back faster on ocean elevations.
        </p>
        <div class="sb-guides">
          <a class="sb-guide" href="/blog/window-washing-santa-barbara-coastal-guide/">
            <strong>Streak-free on the coast</strong><span>The window washing Santa Barbara guide</span>
          </a>
          <a class="sb-guide" href="/blog/screen-cleaning-santa-barbara-coastal-salt-and-oak-pollen-guide/">
            <strong>Salt and oak pollen</strong><span>Screen cleaning in Santa Barbara</span>
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- Service Areas -->
  <section class="areas-section" id="areas">
    <div class="areas-inner">
      <div class="areas-text">
        <h2>Serving Your Neighborhood</h2>
        <p>Locally owned and operated in Ventura County. We know these neighborhoods because we grew up here, Westlake High alumni proudly serving our community.</p>
